67},{"no":747991324,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:12:54","name":"Anonymous","com":"Was this level in the Microsoft Plus Edition on Windows XP? I can&#039;t remember","filename":"sce4b8","ext":".jpg","w":540,"h":720,"tn_w":93,"tn_h":125,"tim":1789780374549885,"time":1789780374,"md5":"wEOHW0o2SJrZ2L4kR3casg==","fsize":75411,"resto":747989067},{"no":747991515,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:16:45","name":"Anonymous","com":"I wish San Francisco was real :(","time":1789780605,"resto":747989067},{"no":747991586,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:18:20","name":"Anonymous","com":"<a href=\"#p747991094\" class=\"quotelink\">&gt;&gt;747991094<\/a><br>Sausalito my beloved.","time":1789780700,"resto":747989067},{"no":747992841,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:43:24","name":"Anonymous","com":"<a href=\"#p747989067\" class=\"quotelink\">&gt;&gt;747989067<\/a>","filename":"Great-Mighty-Poo-Conker","ext":".jpg","w":1024,"h":585,"tn_w":125,"tn_h":71,"tim":1789782204805230,"time":1789782204,"md5":"Bsh8zlDxAbQ7XINp7\/84Nw==","fsize":61658,"resto":747989067}],"last_modified":1789782204},{"no":747956324,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)11:37:39","name":"Anonymous","com":"<span class=\"quote\">&gt;once every year in the US, all crime becomes completely legal for 24 hours <\/span><br><br>Realistically what would you do in this situation?","filename":"purge game","ext":".jpg","w":800,"h":894,"tn_w":223,"tn_h":250,"tim":1789745859402705,"time":1789745859,"md5":"p6dfe\/467UxjIE4G6bBopA==","fsize":103475,"resto":0,"bumplimit":0,"imagelimit":0,"semantic_url":"once-every-year-in-the-us-all-crime-becomes","custom_spoiler":1,"replies":315,"images":32,"omitted_posts":310,"omitted_images":31,"last_replies":[{"no":747992304,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:32:35","name":"Anonymous","com":"<a href=\"#p747956324\" class=\"quotelink\">&gt;&gt;747956324<\/a><br><br>I got grief with this franchise, as it fails to live up to its potential.<br><br>The Purge could be cool. But it&#039;s so baked in champagne liberal ideas and filled with the same hackneyed stereotypes, that I can&#039;t take it seriously. Can&#039;t find it scary. Only vaguely funny at best.<br><br>Case in point: that recent Purge movie ends with our troupe of illegals and based cattle rancher beating up the redneck racists and escaping to Mexico. Where they are accepted with open arms by UN &amp; Mexican border security, likes it&#039;s the Bay Area pride parade.<br><br>If this was a proper horror franchise? It&#039;d be revealed then that the Purge was going worldwide. Absolute chaos unfolding in the cities, as governments and elites around the world were embracing violence to control the populous.<br><br>Cue setting up the sequel for WORLD PURGE.<br><br>But no. It&#039;s just a variant of &quot;white people scary&quot; genre. When it could be so much more scary, in all systems being turnt on the common users. All social trust cannibalizing itself. Horror, as something old and primal once repressed in human nature begins to rear its ugly head again over the shambles of modern civilization. All the while the profiteers just sit back, armed to the teeth on thrones of bone and eating human flesh.<br><br>It could be better.","filename":"1783635879087346","ext":".mp4","w":498,"h":498,"tn_w":125,"tn_h":125,"tim":1789781555998216,"time":1789781555,"md5":"jbgJkT7w61HqhCPh4z8t4g==","fsize":34098,"resto":747956324},{"no":747992426,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:34:56","name":"Anonymous","com":"<a href=\"#p747992304\" class=\"quotelink\">&gt;&gt;747992304<\/a><br>i seem to recall there was an identical straight to tv movie with the exact same premise the Purged ripped off.","time":1789781696,"resto":747956324},{"no":747992623,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:38:39","name":"Anonymous","com":"<a href=\"#p747956405\" class=\"quotelink\">&gt;&gt;747956405<\/a><br><span class=\"quote\">&gt;CEOs<\/span><br>You are on a string, sheep! CEOs are at least trained in how to conduct a business and be held with some ethics. Its board members who are the ones who push the agenda to make money over anything else and are some asshole who got in because they had a lot of money.<br><br>Oh, wait, you&#039;d never get to these board members because everyone of them is off living outside the US in a commie country busy laughing at a livestream as the Purge happens. They laugh because as rich communists they naturally delight at human suffering but also because they were given all that money by their government to fuck up your country (not theirs).","time":1789781919,"resto":747956324},{"no":747992738,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:41:14","name":"Anonymous","com":"<a href=\"#p747956324\" class=\"quotelink\">&gt;&gt;747956324<\/a><br><span class=\"quote\">&gt;one day where people everyone can let loose to &quot;resolve their anger&quot; or something<\/span><br><span class=\"quote\">&gt;but also they cant do anything meaningful, mostly just kill fellow working class <\/span><br><br>wouldnt this just have the opposite effect and make everyone fucking despise the people in power","time":1789782074,"resto":747956324},{"no":747992834,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:43:15","name":"Anonymous","com":"<a href=\"#p747956964\" class=\"quotelink\">&gt;&gt;747956964<\/a><br>Because the bank tellers would all take the day off and the vault wouldnt be opened. You think they wouldn&#039;t take the day off?","time":1789782195,"resto":747956324}],"last_modified":1789782195},{"no":747965283,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)13:54:01","name":"Anonymous","sub":"Mega Man: Dual Override Devs Talk Proto Man, Share New Details","com":"<span class=\"quote\">&gt;You cannot switch between Mega Man and Proto Man during a playthrough. You choose to play as Mega Man or Proto Man at the start of the game.<\/span><br><br><span class=\"quote\">&gt;Stage design between Mega Man and Proto Man is mostly the same, but enemy placement changes between the two campaigns. The team wants players to encounter surprises on a second playthrough rather than already knowing exactly which enemy is coming next.<\/span><br><br><span class=\"quote\">&gt;The team wanted to include Proto Man as a playable character from the start of development, in part due to fan requests. The name Dual Override came later.<\/span><br><br><span class=\"quote\">&gt;Dual Override&#039;s two art directors are Yuji Ishihara and Shinsuke Komaki. For the game&#039;s main visual, Ishihara produced the rough composition and Komaki finished it. Ishihara handled Mega Man while Komaki handled Proto Man.<\/span><br><br><span class=\"quote\">&gt;In past games, character designs have generally balanced &quot;cool&quot; and &quot;cute.&quot; With Dual Override, Ishihara and Komaki pushed things further toward cool, partly to appeal to a broader audience.<\/span><br><br><span class=\"quote\">&gt;While the basic storyline between Mega Man and Proto Man will be the same, the team says Proto Man will have more characterization than usual. Ikuta points out that Proto Man traditionally hasn&#039;t spoken very much, but because he is now a lead protagonist, there will be more opportunities for his personality to shine.<\/span><br><br><span class=\"quote\">&gt;While designing Proto Man, Komaki remembered that he has a faulty power core and began thinking about how to incorporate that into his design. Komaki sketched Proto Man overheating and venting heat, then pitched the idea internally. From there, the art concept became an actual gameplay mechanic, with the planners determining how venting would function in-game.<\/span>","filename":"HSgwLnrWYAIml9-","ext":".jpg","w":1043,"h":637,"tn_w":250,"tn_h":152,"tim":1789754041189734,"time":1789754041,"md5":"zakSpP4Y8rwIiOlcvOBaDA==","fsize":102844,"resto":0,"m_img":1,"bumplimit":0,"imagelimit":0,"semantic_url":"mega-man-dual-override-devs-talk-proto-man-share","custom_spoiler":1,"replies":273,"images":58,"omitted_posts":268,"omitted_images":57,"last_replies":[{"no":747992598,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:38:13","name":"Anonymous","com":"<a href=\"#p747991358\" class=\"quotelink\">&gt;&gt;747991358<\/a><br>maybe tinkering the co-op they did with X dive so that it doesn&#039;t mess with it?","time":1789781893,"resto":747965283},{"no":747992635,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:38:51","name":"Anonymous","com":"<a href=\"#p747991717\" class=\"quotelink\">&gt;&gt;747991717<\/a><br>Unless you are Guts Man, Wily does really care for robots masters in general.<br><br><span class=\"quote\">&gt;Bass how did he only have a battle network<\/span><br>Classic was in sleep mode by the 2000s, BN was also really popular back then, and he also had MM&amp;B &amp; other spin-offs.","time":1789781931,"resto":747965283},{"no":747992651,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:39:14","name":"Anonymous","com":"<a href=\"#p747965283\" class=\"quotelink\">&gt;&gt;747965283<\/a><br>Yes but can you whistle with Blues tho","time":1789781954,"resto":747965283},{"no":747992789,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:42:29","name":"Anonymous","com":"<a href=\"#p747990514\" class=\"quotelink\">&gt;&gt;747990514<\/a><br><span class=\"quote\">&gt;It is because the stage system outdated<\/span><br>No.<br><br>Even Inti Creates who went with the Area system ultimately gave up on it when they made their own IP with Gunvolt and Luminous Striker, going back to them, stages are good and perfect to introduce any gimmick, you are just short sighted.","time":1789782149,"resto":747965283},{"no":747992832,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)21:43:14","name":"Anonymous","com":"I think the hitoshi ariga take on wily is probably the best one ever, still unrepentantly evil, but also with a pragmatic side, a genuine love for robotics, and a unique sense of pride that only shows itself in certain situations.<br>he&#039;s a fun villain.","filename":"wily","ext":".jpg","w":2208,"h":1632,"tn_w":125,"tn_h":92,"tim":1789782194327113,"time":1789782194,"md5":"1g4cmgC0alO6C3EdtNuhtA==","fsize":1289036,"resto":747965283,"m_img":1}],"last_modified":1789782194},{"no":747936015,"now":"09\/18\/26(Fri)03:57:53","name":"Anonymous","sub":"Marvel&#039;s &quot;Wolverine&quot;